-- title:
--   Uniqueness of good points reading the same place, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to $q=3$ (`hq3`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). Write $\kappa=\operatorname{ResidueField} A$.
--
--   Three function fields occur. $\bar F_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the intermediate field of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images (under `coeffEmb`) of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`; $\bar F=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` is the analogous base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and over $\kappa$ there are the reduced fields `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\kappa$ generated by the series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) and `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$). Here `Place K F` means a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, with its order function `ord`, its evaluation `evalAt` through the residue field, and rationality meaning surjectivity of $K\to$ residue field.
--
--   The data and hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`: the rational places $w$ that are affine geometric places and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with invariant $j$ has no non-trivial $q$-torsion affine point.
--
--   *Reduction of the level-$M'$ field.* `hle` is the inclusion $\bar F_{M'}\le\bar F$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\bar F_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ (an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is integral exactly when it lies in $A$, and its residue is its residue in $\kappa$), the scaling property that every non-zero $f$ has a constant multiple with non-zero residue, and compatibility of divisor push-forward with orders. `hR₀` requires this reduction to be coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that image is in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   *Igusa branches.* $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$. Four hypotheses govern it: `hIg_inf` identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$, for $\ell_\infty=$ `lineInfty q`, as the Gauss ring — $f$ belongs to it exactly when $f=x/y$ for Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is non-zero; `hIg` says that every line $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}(q)(\gamma)\cdot\ell_\infty$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   *Supersingular valuation rings.* $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each $s\in W$, subject to four hypotheses. `hSS_A`: an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over`: for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of `coeffEmb ℚ̄ jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *Regular prolongation.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and satisfying the same scaling property), with `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$. `hR₀O`: $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$.
--
--   *Uniformisers and the coefficient field.* $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and lies in $A$ (`hπ`, `hπP`). $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with an element $\pi_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and root of unity.* $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *The finite layer.* $K_1$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and $A_1$ is a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting precisely of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is a further universally quantified statement, with $k_0$ acting on $\bar F$ through $k_0\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F$. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $\bar F/k_0$ such that: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series lies in the image of `coeffEmb ℚ̄`. Put $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion of $A_1\subset K_1\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into $\bar F$, let $j_1\in T_1$ be an element whose image in $\bar F$ is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of `coeffEmb ℚ̄ jq` (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant), and let $j_1\neq 0$. Let $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a finite set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` such that every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ has image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, and such that $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ exactly when for some $s\in W$ one has, for all $g$, that $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in that of $Q$.
--
--   On the scheme $\mathfrak X=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` (the $A_1$-subalgebras of $T_1$ of elements integral over $A_1[j_1]$, respectively $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with the canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` into $\mathfrak X$ and the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, the statement introduces the following predicates.
--
--   `InStalk x f`, for $x\in\mathfrak X$ and $f\in T_1$: for every point $y$ of the finite chart with `ιFin`-image $x$ there are elements $g,h$ of `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\,h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise at every point of the infinite chart with `ιInf`-image $x$. `InMax x f`: the same, with the additional requirement $g\in y$ in both clauses.
--
--   `Centred P x`, for $P$ a place of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational, and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`.
--
--   `GoodPt x`: the `toBase`-image of $x$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself, i.e. $x\rightsquigarrow y$ implies $y=x$; at every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; the same for the infinite chart; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi($ `jChartFin` $)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   `Reads x Q`, for $Q$ a place of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$: every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit there if and only if `InMax x f`.
--
--   `OffBranch x`: for every line $\ell\neq\ell_\infty$, at every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$ there is an element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$, and likewise at every point of the infinite chart over $x$.
--
--   The asserted conclusion is a uniqueness statement: for all points $x,x'$ of $\mathfrak X$ with `GoodPt x` and `GoodPt x'`, and every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` with `Reads x Q` and `Reads x' Q`, the equality $x=x'$ holds. The conclusion involves neither $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ nor the predicates `Centred` and `OffBranch`, which are introduced alongside.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the dictionary between closed points of the two-chart integral model of the level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$ and places of the reduced Igusa component, in the case $q=3$: a point lying over the closed point of the base, on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and away from supersingular $j$-invariants is determined by the place of the reduced $X_H$-field that it reads. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three) in the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$.
